# Remove All Whitespace from a String in Java

Here are several approaches to remove all whitespace from a string in Java:

## Method 1: Using `replaceAll()` with Regex

```java
public class RemoveWhitespace {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String original = "Hello World, this is Java!";

        // \\s matches any whitespace character (spaces, tabs, newlines, etc.)
        String result = original.replaceAll("\\s", "");

        System.out.println("Original: " + original);
        System.out.println("Result:   " + result);
    }
}
```

**Output:**
```
Original: Hello World, this is Java!
Result:   HelloWorld,thisisJava!
```

## Method 2: Using `replace()` Method (Spaces Only)

```java
public class RemoveSpaces {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String original = "Hello World Java";
        String result = original.replace(" ", "");

        System.out.println("Result: " + result);
    }
}
```

## Method 3: Using StringBuilder (Manual Iteration)

```java
public class RemoveWhitespaceLoop {
    public static String removeWhitespace(String str) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();

        for (int i = 0; i < str.length(); i++) {
            char ch = str.charAt(i);
            if (!Character.isWhitespace(ch)) {
                sb.append(ch);
            }
        }

        return sb.toString();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String original = "Hello\tWorld\n Java ";
        String result = removeWhitespace(original);

        System.out.println("Original: [" + original + "]");
        System.out.println("Result:   [" + result + "]");
    }
}
```

## Method 4: Using Java 8 Streams

```java
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class RemoveWhitespaceStream {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String original = "Hello World Java 8";

        String result = original.chars()
                .filter(c -> !Character.isWhitespace(c))
                .collect(StringBuilder::new,
                         StringBuilder::appendCodePoint,
                         StringBuilder::append)
                .toString();

        System.out.println("Result: " + result);
    }
}
```

## Complete Example with User Input

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class WhitespaceRemover {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter a string: ");
        String input = scanner.nextLine();

        String result = input.replaceAll("\\s+", "");

        System.out.println("String without whitespace: " + result);
        System.out.println("Original length: " + input.length());
        System.out.println("New length: " + result.length());

        scanner.close();
    }
}
```

## Comparison of Methods

| Method | Removes | Best For |
|--------|---------|----------|
| `replaceAll("\\s", "")` | All whitespace (space, tab, newline, etc.) | Most common use case |
| `replace(" ", "")` | Only spaces | Simple space removal |
| Manual loop | All whitespace | When you need custom logic |
| Streams | All whitespace | Functional programming style |

**Recommended:** Use `replaceAll("\\s", "")` for the most concise and reliable solution that handles all types of whitespace characters.

